          <p style={{ fontSize: 13, color: T.muted, lineHeight: 1.7, marginBottom: 0 }}>
            Neurath wanted factory workers with no statistical training to read his charts
            instantly. His Isotype system used one symbol per unit — no axes, no scales, just
            counting. A row of ten people means ten people. The reader doesn't decode;
            they count. This is the most democratic form of data visualization ever invented.
          </p>
          <WikiLink href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isotype_(picture_language)" label="Isotype picture language" />
          <DivePrompt prompt="Create an Isotype unit chart where one symbol = one unit. Arrange symbols in rows. Use a single shape (circle or square) repeated. Black + one accent color. No axes, no gridlines. The count is the chart." />
          <KeyLesson text="One symbol = one unit. If the reader has to decode your encoding, you've already lost them. The most powerful chart is the one that needs no explanation." />
        </div>
      }
      chart={
        <div style={{ background: T.fg, padding: "20px 20px 14px" }}>
          {loading ? (
            <div style={{ height: 200, background: "#333", borderRadius: 4 }} />
